From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:03:37 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: isp: Zero the lens shading strides of H17
 setfiles

The firmware's lens shading thread (FlowLSC200) faulted on every
CH_SET_FILE_LOAD on T6040, printing "SetLSParamFullImage baseHi
R=120" where macOS prints R=0, and reading 0xf00000 past the setfile.

A setfile is a chain of { size, 0, tag, payload } sections, and the
lens shading tables are described by 18-byte records whose fifth
halfword is the row stride (2 * width) in the xx24 setfiles. The H17
firmware reads that halfword as the high half of the table offset.
Apple's xx25 setfiles are their xx24 twins with exactly these
halfwords zeroed (7524 -> 7525 and 8824 -> 8825 match byte for byte
apart from the header version), and only xx24 files exist for the
IMX958 module, so macOS must zero them as well.

Do the same for H17 firmware after copying the setfile. Setfiles
that already have the field zeroed are left alone.

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Goyvaerts <jonathan.goyvaerts@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit ed7b2a4d3a7fd460be26e1dc6e1688ac2ee07ab4)
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c | 45 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 45 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c
index 5090ed2ed5..24d8a10f4b 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c
@@ -334,6 +334,49 @@ int apple_isp_detect_camera(struct apple_isp *isp)
 	return err;
 }
 
+/*
+ * A setfile is a chain of { le32 size, le32 0, le32 tag, payload } sections
+ * from 0x14 on, size counting what follows it. The lens shading sections
+ * hold 18-byte table records after a 10-byte header: { ?, 0x20, 0x20,
+ * offset lo, offset hi, 0, 0, width, height }. The xx24 setfiles keep the
+ * row stride (2 * width) in "offset hi"; the H17 firmware reads it as the
+ * offset's high half ("baseHi") and faults far past the file. Their xx25
+ * twins are the same tables with it zeroed, as macOS hands them over.
+ */
+static void isp_setfile_fixup_h17(void *data, size_t len)
+{
+	size_t off = 0x14;
+
+	while (off + 12 <= len) {
+		u32 size = get_unaligned_le32(data + off);
+		size_t end = off + 4 + size;
+		size_t rec;
+		int i;
+
+		if (size < 8 || end > len)
+			break;
+
+		switch (get_unaligned_le32(data + off + 8)) {
+		case 0xc003:
+		case 0xc01b:
+		case 0xc01c:
+		case 0xc01f:
+		case 0xc021:
+			rec = off + 12 + 10;
+			for (i = 0; i < 16 && rec + 18 <= end; i++, rec += 18) {
+				if (get_unaligned_le16(data + rec + 2) != 0x20 ||
+				    get_unaligned_le16(data + rec + 4) != 0x20)
+					break;
+				if (get_unaligned_le16(data + rec + 8) ==
+				    2 * get_unaligned_le16(data + rec + 14))
+					put_unaligned_le16(0, data + rec + 8);
+			}
+			break;
+		}
+		off = end;
+	}
+}
+
 static int isp_ch_load_setfile(struct apple_isp *isp, u32 ch)
 {
 	struct isp_format *fmt = isp_get_format(isp, ch);
@@ -372,6 +415,8 @@ static int isp_ch_load_setfile(struct apple_isp *isp, u32 ch)
 	memcpy(isp->data_surf->virt, fw->data, len);
 	memset(isp->data_surf->virt + len, 0, setfile->size - len);
 	release_firmware(fw);
+	if (isp->hw->fw_abi == ISP_FW_ABI_H17)
+		isp_setfile_fixup_h17(isp->data_surf->virt, len);
 
 	return isp_cmd_ch_set_file_load(isp, ch, isp->data_surf->iova,
 					setfile->size);
